  "source": "BUPERSINST 1610.10H CH-2 (26 May 2026 compilation), enclosure (2)",
  "notes": "Reviewed patterns for possible prohibited or sensitive comments in narrative blocks. Matching is on whole lower-case words; '*' ends a word prefix; hyphens and punctuation separate words and a trailing 's is dropped. 'near' requires one of its terms within 'within' words of the match; 'unless' suppresses a match when one of its terms touches the match or its near term. Findings are review prompts (Needs review), never edits or blocks. Severity: 'Needs review' for BUPERSINST prohibitions, 'Information' for application checks (protected characteristics, political activity, personal identifiers, all capitals). An unless term starting with < counts only before the match, up to twice as far away (duty verbs: 'screened 400 Sailors for hypertension'). Each match group has a stable id (rule.suffix) used to turn it off in a workspace; 'why' is the plain-language reason shown in the Content checks window.",
